  "query_preview": "..\n(Tomorrow through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1136 AM CDT Wed Oct 21 2026\n\nOverall, the forecast remains fairly uneventful through the \nremainder of the forecast period. High pressure will maintain dry \nconditions with slightly warmer temperatures in the upper 70s and \nlower 80s through this weekend. The ridge will gradually slide \neast as we move into next week, with southwest flow developing \noverhead as a trough lifts east-northeastward into the plains. \nPrecipitation chances increase over the local area Monday into \nTuesday, though rainfall amounts appear fairly light at this time.\nA northern stream trough will swing through the northern plains \nthereafter, potentially sending a cold front toward our area mid \nto late next week.\n\nAfternoon winds will tend to increase Friday and this weekend \n(10-20 mph) which may locally increase fire weather concerns, \nespecially northwest of I-44 where gusts up to 25 mph will be \npossible. Otherwise, low-impact, pleasant weather is generally \nexpected over the next several days, with temperatures running \nseveral degrees above average.",
